# Build context excludes. The build context is the MONOREPO ROOT for every
# service (workspace packages are consumed as raw TypeScript), so this file has
# to cover every app and package at once.
#
# NOTE THE `**/` PREFIXES — they are not decoration. Docker matches these
# patterns against the full path relative to the context root, so a bare
# `node_modules` excludes ONLY the top-level directory and happily copies
# `apps/api/node_modules`, `packages/db/node_modules` and the rest. That is not
# a size problem, it is a correctness one: this repo is developed on Windows,
# pnpm writes ABSOLUTE symlinks into `.pnpm`, and a `COPY . .` would drop those
# dead links on top of the install the image just did — the exact "never copy
# host node_modules" trap. It fails as MODULE_NOT_FOUND during `prisma generate`.

# Dependencies — always reinstalled inside the image.
**/node_modules

# Build outputs — regenerated in the build stage.
**/.next
**/dist
**/.turbo
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Version control
.git

# Local secrets. The images take configuration from the environment; a stray
# .env baked into a layer is both wrong and a leak.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Playwright artifacts
apps/e2e/test-results
apps/e2e/playwright-report
